# {{project_name}}

Generated with `uvx vision-agents init`. See the docs at <https://visionagents.ai>.

## Setup

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the keys.
2. Install dependencies:

   ```bash
   uv sync
   ```

3. Run the agent:

   ```bash
   uv run agent.py run     # single-call console
   uv run agent.py serve   # HTTP server
   ```

4. Run the tests:

   ```bash
   uv run pytest
   ```

5. Optionally, simulate conversations. Switch the agent to a text LLM such as
   `gemini.LLM()` (realtime LLMs cannot be simulated), describe each conversation
   in a `scenarios/*.toml` file and run:

   ```bash
   uv run agent.py simulate scenarios/
   ```

## Docker

```bash
docker build -t {{project_name}} .
docker run --env-file .env -p 8000:8000 {{project_name}}
```
